Wave 1's criterion applied again: what is deleted carries no rule; what is
kept stays on the baseline with its reason stated, never laundered.

Deleted (each a restatement of an API the crate already publishes):
`grant_by_id` - `grants()` iterates the same map and `is_valid(id, block)`
answers the only question worth asking of it; `Disposition::is_fix` - a
one-variant `matches!()` wrapper over the enum whose variants are the
actual API (its test now names `Some(Disposition::Fixed(_))`, the fact
it checked); `read::is_known` - `PerceptionKind::parse(tag).is_some()` is
the closed list, the wrapper restated it; `anlama::found_in_data` - the
public `attachments()` reader plus `Attachment::mentions` say exactly
this, and the test says it in those words now. Four items, 331 tests held
- no test left, two were rewritten to speak through the live surface,
which is the whole difference between shrinking and amputating.

Kept, each a sole carrier the gate correctly still records: `open_path`
(the chain's documented path step - without it `run` has nothing to
check), `submit`/`peek_due`/`evictions` (kuyruk's entry and its README-named
ledger), `declare_wired`/`declare_unwired`/`unclaimed` (the whole public
reason takip exists), `with_capability`/`with_symbol`/`reject_names`/
`record_of`/`with_attachment`/`with_entries` (sole setters and readers of
rules enforced elsewhere), `from_hex`/`to_hex` (the only codec pair for
the id type - no Display to collapse into), `is_finalized` (muhur's
sealed-chain question), `compact` (index's line in the crate table is
literally "deterministic context compaction" - either it gets wired or
the row is retold, and that is a decision for the wiring wave, not a
delete key). `jsonrpc_request`/`to_corpus_line` stay queued as the known
chain-debt item (the same queue entry that owes bud_aiGetCeilings its
client) - they are the plumbing that wiring will call, named where the
queue already tracks it.

The read-back caught what no gate here can: all four deletions had left
their own doc comments (and two `#[must_use]` attributes) stranded on the
item below them - an attribute on a module, two merged doc lines
describing functions that no longer exist, and in denetim a truly empty
impl block that would not have compiled. This sandbox has no compiler
(measured): the fix was reading every deleted region's context, and the
brace scan across the touched files. Floor 25 -> 21, measured 21/21; all
24 cargo-free gates green; `chain-surface-fixed` red reproduced identical
at the base, unchanged queue debt.
